<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="062" project="spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>F1 — `/office/search/entities` is a live app-only enumeration of every Matter, Project, Invoice, Account and Contact with no security trimming</title>
    <phase>5 Remediation — authorization</phase>
    <gate>blocked — requires 061 (the census must govern this route before it is changed)</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <completion date="2026-09-21" note="projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/notes/062-entity-search-trim.md">
      Mechanism: impersonated Dataverse read (MSCRMCallerID) via the existing IImpersonatedCommunicationQuery
      seam + ICallerSystemUserResolver — Dataverse trims inside the query, so all five entity types and every
      page are covered with zero added round trips. Post-trim per row (task 032's mechanism) was considered
      and rejected on latency (up to 250 round trips on a 500 ms typeahead) and coverage (its shared
      allow-list has no account/contact entry). Reproduce-first RED recorded verbatim; the 8-test contract
      suite seeded RED 7/1 and restored GREEN 8/0. NOT MET, recorded rather than implied: criterion
      "task 061's guard no longer flags this route" (061 deferred; the guard governs no Office route today),
      and no live-Dataverse verification — the BFF app user's prvActOnBehalfOfAnotherUser Delegate privilege
      must be confirmed before deploy.
    </completion>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Security fix on a LIVE route that the add-in pane depends on. Tags include bff-api + auth + security. Changing the identity a Dataverse query runs under is a behaviour change for every caller.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Security-sensitive, and the correct mechanism (run OBO vs post-trim through AuthorizationService) is a genuine design judgment with different performance and correctness profiles. The pane depends on this route, so a wrong choice breaks a shipped surface.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Edits `OfficeService.cs` — hot path shared with 058/059/063/064/065 and with unified-access-control-r2.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>061</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, api, auth, authorization, security, office, dataverse, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>6-10 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>`GET /office/search/entities` runs an app-only Dataverse query with no per-user security trimming, returning every Matter, Project, Invoice, Account and Contact to any authenticated caller. Make the results reflect what the caller is actually allowed to see.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. This is the highest-severity live finding in the project — treat it as a security fix, not a feature change.</role>

  <goal>`/office/search/entities` returns only records the calling user is authorized to read, proven by a negative test in which a user without rights on a matter cannot see that matter in results.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Found 2026-09-21 by the Fable model-level review (`notes/fable-review-2026-09-21.md` §2, finding F1).
      **Rated HIGH — the only finding with a live, exploitable consequence today.**

      Route mapped at `OfficeEndpoints.cs:999-1008`. Filter chain is `AddOfficeRateLimitFilter` +
      `AddOfficeAuthFilter` **only** — no per-resource check of any kind. Handler `:1064-1177` passes the
      caller's `q` straight through.

      The service confirms it in its own comment, `OfficeService.cs:1652-1653`:

          app-only read (no per-user security trimming yet)

      The query at `:1699-1735` runs over the singleton app-only `DataverseWebApiClient` (`:54-57`).

      **What a caller gets**: names, numbers, descriptions, GUIDs and `modifiedon` for **all** records of five
      types — Matter, Project, Invoice, Account, Contact — including secure matters they have no rights to,
      50 per type per page, with `skip` paging to walk the whole table.

      **What they need**: a valid token and a two-character substring.

      **Why it is the keystone.** Findings F2 (`send-to-index`), F3 (`/office/todo`) and F4 (unassociated
      `/save`) all require a record GUID to act on. This route hands them out in bulk. Fixing F1 does not fix
      those — they have their own tasks — but leaving F1 open makes each of them materially easier to exploit.

      **Pre-existing on master**, not introduced by this project. We own it because we found it, the pane is a
      caller (`matterTypeLookupService.ts:9` and the "Related to" picker), and the owner has directed that
      review findings be fixed in this project rather than deferred.

      **The pane depends on this route.** A fix that returns nothing, or that is materially slower, breaks the
      entity picker — a shipped surface. Verify the picker still works.
    </background>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="this task">MUST NOT close the gap by removing the route. The pane uses it. This is a trim, not a deletion.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-008">Where a per-resource check belongs in a filter, put it in a filter. Where trimming must happen inside the query, document why in the code.</constraint>
    <constraint source="this task">Every result path added or modified in this task applies the same trim — including the paging path. A trim that only covers page 1 is not a trim.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Add the negative authorization test at a KEEP path. Follow the shape of `VisualizationRowAuthorizationContractTests.cs`, which task 032 wrote for exactly this class of defect.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Report publish-size delta against a FRESH `origin/master` build. Run the CVE check.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">REPRODUCE-FIRST: before changing behaviour, write a probe proving a user WITHOUT rights on a specific matter receives that matter from `/office/search/entities`. Record the observed response verbatim in the task note. This is the evidence the gap was real.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Results are trimmed to the caller's rights — either by running the query as the caller (OBO / `MSCRMCallerID`) or by post-trimming each row through `AuthorizationService`. State which mechanism was chosen and why in the task note and in a code comment.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NEGATIVE TEST (the gate): given a user with no read rights on matter X, when they search a substring matching X, then X is absent from the response — while a permitted neighbour record IS present, and the returned count matches the trimmed row set. Copy the assertion shape from `VisualizationRowAuthorizationContractTests.cs`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">SEED THE NEGATIVE TEST: disable the trim and show the test goes RED; restore and show GREEN. Record both outputs. A test that has not been seen to fail proves nothing — this is the lesson from task 056's gate.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The paging path is trimmed too: a `skip` beyond page 1 returns no unauthorized row. Cover this explicitly.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All five entity types are covered — Matter, Project, Invoice, Account, Contact. A trim applied to four of five is a gap.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The false comment at `OfficeService.cs:1652-1653` is removed or replaced with one that describes what the code now does.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Task 061's guard no longer flags this route.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The pane's entity picker still works: the "Related to" picker and `matterTypeLookupService.ts` both return results for an authorized user. Verify and record.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Full BFF suite green; report the count and reconcile against 12,379 passed / 0 failed. ArchTests green. Publish size and CVE reported.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the trim contract, the negative case, the paging case, the five entity types and the seed directions named above. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the task note.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If per-caller trimming makes the picker unusably slow (a p95 materially worse than today's), STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6 with the measured numbers and the options. Do NOT silently ship a slow picker, and do NOT silently keep the untrimmed query because trimming was inconvenient.</trigger>
    <trigger>If Dataverse cannot express the trim for one of the five entity types, STOP and escalate rather than shipping a partial trim that looks complete.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step>/conflict-check (bff-api hot path).</step>
    <step>Reproduce the gap and record the evidence verbatim.</step>
    <step>Read `VisualizationRowAuthorizationContractTests.cs` and `notes/032-authorization-hardening.md` — task 032 solved this exact class of problem on another route; copy its mechanism where it fits.</step>
    <step>Choose the trim mechanism, write down why, implement it across all five types and the paging path.</step>
    <step>Write the negative test. Seed it both directions and record the outputs.</step>
    <step>Verify the pane's picker still works.</step>
    <step>Build, full suite, ArchTests, publish size, CVE.</step>
    <step>Write `notes/062-entity-search-trim.md`. Update TASK-INDEX.md: 062 → ✅.</step>
  </steps>

